  "query_preview": "..\n\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Mainly Dry/pleasant today and Wed. Highs in the\nupper 70s to the lower 80s both days...albeit a bit more humid \nWed. \n\nA ridge of high pressure in place will result in a beautiful day of \nweather today. A moisture starved northern stream coupled with \ndiurnal heating will result in scattered clouds today...But \nstill expect plenty of sunshine too. While we can not rule out\nthe risk for a brief spot sprinkle/light shower in the afternoon...areal\ncoverage and duration would be so limited it is not worth \nincluding in the forecast. High temps will mainly be in the \nupper 70s to the lower 80s with comfortable humidity levels too.\nLow temps tonight should drop into the middle 50s to the lower \n60s with light/calm winds along with just some scattered to \nbroken mid level cloudiness. \n\nHigh pressure moves off the mid-Atlantic coast by Wed. Highs will \nagain be in the upper 70s to the lower 80s...but it will be a bit \nmore humid as high pressure moving off the mid-Atlantic coast brings \nincreasing low level moisture. We also do expect a bit of a \nsouthwest breeze to develop by mid to late afternoon. \n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...Breezy, warm, and humid Wed night into Thu with\nbrief scattered showers possible...but the vast majority of \nthis time will be dry. \n\nA cold front will approach the region Wed night into early Thu. Out \nahead of this front a modest southwest LLJ of 45-50+ knots at 950 \nmb. This should be enough to result in breezy southwest wind gusts \nof 20-30 mph with a few gusts of 35-40 mph possible in the vicinity \nof the upper Cape where they are favored based on soundings and \npattern recognition. \n\nAs for precipitation chances...Pwats will approach 2 inches ahead of \nthe cold front. However...the low level moisture is fairly shallow \nand only deepens in a narrow band along the cold front and the \nbetter dynamics/forcing is across northern New England. \nTherefore...only expect a brief round of scattered showers with the \ncold front and the majority of Wed night into Thu will feature dry \nweather. It will be a humid though and the gusty southwest \nwinds will hold low temps into the 65-70 degree range Wed night.\nHighs on Thu will be warm for this time of year...mainly in the\nmiddle 80s but a few spots may reach the upper 80s and it will\nbe humid.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 3...Mainly dry/pleasant with lower humidity Fri into Sat \nwith highs mainly in the 70s. Turning a bit more humid/warmer Sun \ninto Mon.\n\nPost frontal airmass will result in beautiful weather Fri into Sat \nwith lower humidity. Plenty of sunshine expected both days with \nhighs mainly in the 70s along with comfortable humidity. High \npressure overhead will allow for many locations to fall into the 40s \nto the lower 50s Fri night/Sat am...which may end up being the \ncoolest night for many locations since late last spring. \n\nThis high pressure system will shift east of the region by Sun and \nMon. This will allow for a return southwest flow of a bit more \nhumid/warmer airmass to work back into the region.",
